# MenuFlow — local development environment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the two Supabase values below.
# .env.local is gitignored (`.env*`) — never commit real credentials there.
#
# Fill in from your Supabase project:
#   Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API
#     Project URL        -> NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL
#     Publishable key    -> NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY  (sb_publishable_...)
#
# Leaving both blank is safe: lib/supabase.js deliberately falls back to a
# no-op client and the app runs on data/menu.json seed data instead
# (supabaseReady === false). A half-filled or wrong value is worse than
# leaving it blank — supabaseReady becomes true and the app tries to reach a
# host that doesn't exist.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL="https://YOUR_SUPABASE_PROJECT.supabase.co"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="sb_publishable_YOUR_KEY"
# Legacy JWT anon key — only needed if your project still issues one instead
# of a publishable key. lib/supabase.js checks PUBLISHABLE_KEY first, then
# falls back to this.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="YOUR_ANON_KEY"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database and Edge Functions are NOT configured through this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Schema (supabase/migrations/*.sql) and Edge Functions (supabase/functions/)
# are applied through the Supabase MCP server (`apply_migration` /
# `deploy_edge_function`), not the SQL editor and not the Supabase CLI — see
# CLAUDE.md's "Commands" section. There is no self-service sign-up anywhere
# in this app: account creation is super-admin-only, end-to-end (a restaurant
# and its admin login are created together from /superadmin via the
# create-restaurant-user Edge Function). To bootstrap the first super_admin:
#   1. Have that person sign in once via any flow that creates an auth.users
#      row (or create one directly in the Supabase Dashboard), then
#   2. update public.profiles set role = 'super_admin' where email = '...';
#
# /admin, /staff and /superadmin are protected server-side by middleware.js
# (checks the Supabase session + role on every request, before the page
# renders) — this requires session cookies rather than localStorage, which is
# why lib/supabase.js uses @supabase/ssr's createBrowserClient.
#
# Password reset: /login has a "Şifrəni unutmusunuz?" link that emails a
# recovery link to /reset-password. In Supabase dashboard > Authentication >
# URL Configuration, add {your-domain}/reset-password to Redirect URLs, or
# the email link will be rejected.
#
# Email confirmations: if Authentication > Providers > Email > "Confirm
# email" is ON (recommended), new accounts must click the link Supabase
# emails them before they can log in.
#
# POS integration secrets (supabase/migrations/0026_pos_integration.sql,
# 0027_pos_order_push_observability.sql) are provisioned as Supabase Edge
# Function secrets and a Vault entry — NOT as values in this file:
#   - POS_ORDER_PUSH_SECRET: set via `supabase secrets set` or the Dashboard
#     on the pos-poster-order-push function, matching the value stored in
#     Vault as 'pos_order_push_secret'. See that migration's own comment for
#     the exact provisioning steps.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Apple Pay merchant ID — lib/services/paymentService.js reads it.
# Unset falls back to 'merchant.menuflow.demo'. Note: NO real payment
# processor is wired in either way — this only opens the wallet sheet and
# collects a token; see paymentService.js's own header comment.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APPLE_PAY_MERCHANT_ID="merchant.yourcompany.menuflow"

# Needed only if Supabase Dashboard -> Authentication -> Attack Protection
# has Cloudflare Turnstile or hCaptcha enabled.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY="YOUR_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY"

# Web Push (StaffApp.jsx "Enable notifications", 0030_push_notifications.sql).
# This is the PUBLIC half of a VAPID key pair only — safe to expose
# client-side, not a secret. Generate a pair once with:
#   npx web-push generate-vapid-keys
# The private half is never set here — it's a notify-push Edge Function
# secret (VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY), alongside VAPID_SUBJECT (a mailto: or https:
# URL identifying you) and PUSH_NOTIFY_SECRET (the same shared-secret
# pattern as POS_ORDER_PUSH_SECRET above, provisioned via Vault — see
# 0030's own trailing comment for the exact one-time command).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY="YOUR_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY"
